WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.530
- All right, we always like to close out

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:02.730
with something uplifting.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.151
Here's today's What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.151 --> 00:00:07.459
(upbeat music playing)

00:00:07.459 --> 00:00:09.960
So, you may remember this time last year,

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.640
we did a primetime holiday special

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.250
called Kelly Clarkson Presents:
When Christmas Comes Around,

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.200
Um, I got to sing with some great artists,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.790
and performed some of
my own holiday songs.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:18.623
It was fun, but we also

00:00:18.623 --> 00:00:21.219
featured some very special everyday people

00:00:21.219 --> 00:00:23.010
lifting up their hometowns.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.240
They're incredible.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.190
Do y'all remember Dr. Giles Willis

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.630
and the surprise Melissa McCarthy

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.183
and I were able to gift him?

00:00:31.241 --> 00:00:32.392
- Growing up in this community,

00:00:32.392 --> 00:00:34.020
I didn't know what a
dentist's office even looked

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:37.290
like until I actually
had my first toothache.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:39.540
So I got some tweezers, then I tried to go

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.820
into my mouth to pull
out what was hurting me.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.650
My mom comes in and says, you
know, "What are you doing?"

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.240
And I was like, I'm trying
to get this tooth out.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.267
And finally she said,

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:47.910
"We have to go to the dentist tomorrow."

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.800
I realized right then that no child

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.960
at eight years old should
have to go through that pain

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.420
and that put me on my trajectory now.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.680
- Years later, Giles attended

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.570
Howard University Dental School

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:00.990
and went on to open his first
practice in North Carolina.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.100
- All through dental schools and stuff,

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.140
I was thinking of how I could help people.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:05.880
It just so happened
that I was home one day

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.022
and I asked my mom about
the actual building

00:01:08.022 --> 00:01:10.470
that I had my tooth pulled in

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.060
and she said there was
a For Sale sign on it.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.830
I called a number and
purchased it immediately.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.260
This was the actual room
where I had my tooth

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.650
extracted that day that
started this whole thing.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.290
- We know that you wanna open
a clinic by the new year.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.700
Do you think, how is that going?

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.200
Do you think that's gonna be possible?

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.100
- I'm trying really hard.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:26.940
It's a labor of love.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.290
I'm trying really hard.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.540
People need to need it
really bad in our community.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:31.770
So, I hope I do.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.600
- Ah well, it's Christmas time,

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.030
so let's get you closer to your dream.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.280
That is the the gift today
that we wanna give to you.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.380
Together, Wayfair, my good neighbor

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.804
Melissa McCarthy and I are giving you

00:01:42.804 --> 00:01:45.090
- $100,000 for the clinic.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:46.744
- What?

00:01:46.744 --> 00:01:47.975
Yeah!

00:01:47.975 --> 00:01:52.516
- You are kidding me.

00:01:52.516 --> 00:01:54.212
(applause)

00:01:54.212 --> 00:01:55.897
- Love his reaction.

00:01:55.897 --> 00:01:58.703
Dr. Giles indeed has
opened that new practice

00:01:58.703 --> 00:02:00.690
and we have him on the line right now.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.529
What's up Dr. Giles?

00:02:02.529 --> 00:02:03.645
(applause)

00:02:03.645 --> 00:02:04.478
- Hello Kelly.

00:02:04.478 --> 00:02:05.646
How are you doing?

00:02:05.646 --> 00:02:07.050
- Merry Christmas.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:10.530
So since I saw you last, the
new practice is open, right?

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.660
- Kelly, the new practice is open.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.177
Thankfully, I am swamped.

00:02:14.177 --> 00:02:16.006
I am seeing a ton of people.

00:02:16.006 --> 00:02:18.120
Thanks to you and your wonderful gift.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:21.780
Last year, I was able to pay
off the rest of the debt.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.360
When you actually gave
me that wonderful gift,

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.800
I was able to buy a scanner.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.170
I was able to get my panoramic machine

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:32.670
and all three of my rooms are
active, ready to go, pay for.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:36.090
I've been able to do a lot in
the community thanks to that.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:41.090
I also was able to get
a Community Hero award

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.260
which still feels kind of funny

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.970
to me cause I don't feel like a hero.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.650
I just feel like a
person who wants to work

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.360
in his community to make it better.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.470
- Aw, that's amazing.

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:51.420
Thank you so much Dr. Giles.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.220
Wishing you a very merry Christmas.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.053
All right?

00:02:54.053 --> 00:02:54.990
(applause)

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.150
- And thank you again.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:56.983
I appreciate it.

00:02:56.983 --> 00:02:59.733
- Absolutely. I'm liking
your post right now.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.910
Alright, so we've hit that point

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.100
when we usually give our
guest a thousand dollars,

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.330
thanks to our season long partner,

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.800
Pilot Pen Makers of the Frixion,

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.108
the Go-To Erasable Pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:03:10.108 --> 00:03:13.680
But today we've got a Kelly
extra helping of Christmas

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:14.880
for someone in the audience.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.310
So there's a check under
one of your chairs.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.360
So go ahead and look.

00:03:19.785 --> 00:03:22.118
(drum roll)

00:03:25.316 --> 00:03:27.566
(applause)

00:03:31.449 --> 00:03:32.830
Stand up

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:34.820
What? What's your name?

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.237
What's your name?

00:03:36.237 --> 00:03:37.740
- Oh, I'm Nadia.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.000
- Nadia, what do you think you'll do

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.620
with a thousand dollars?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.340
- Pay off some of my student loans.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:43.530
(laughing)

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.480
- You're, I feel like you're

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.910
like the fifth person to
come here and say that.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.620
Student loans are an issue, people.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:50.790
So here's the thing.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:51.630
Totally do that.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.010
Just take a tiny bit but out though

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.180
to do something fun for yourself.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:55.053
I'm just saying.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:56.963
- Thank you so much.

00:03:56.963 --> 00:03:57.796
- Yeah, I hope you enjoy it.

00:03:57.796 --> 00:03:58.629
Merry Christmas, Nadia!

00:03:58.629 --> 00:03:59.645
- Merry Christmas to you too!

00:03:59.645 --> 00:04:00.478
Thank You!

00:04:00.478 --> 00:04:01.800
Thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.590
Mrs. Michelle Obama,
Dolly Parton, Amy Poller

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.430
and Matthew West.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.468
Y'all have a great day.

00:04:06.468 --> 00:04:08.218
and if it's not, try and change it.

